(1194350, 148986, 19010, '<td valign="top">This was shot too late in the day. I feel that it is to dark to make the a statement. Nothing realy tends to stand out.  I am not even sure what the red thing is or if the foot prints are supppose to be part of the separation.. so jsut too dark for me to fully grasp it''s meaning.</td>', 'This was shot too late in the day. I feel that it is to dark to make the a statement. Nothing realy tends to stand out.  I am not even sure what the red thing is or if the foot prints are supppose to be part of the separation.. so jsut too dark for me to fully grasp it''s meaning.', '2005-02-25 13:46:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1194417, 148919, 19010, '<td valign="top">This is a very tastefull and interesting use of a common theme in this challenge. I love the way you use the grapes and plater to enhance the image. You have definately steped this them up a notch. I would liked to have seen a little more light on the grapes.  I also don''t particularly like the separation beteen table and wall. Overall this is a great shot keep up the nice work.</td>', 'This is a very tastefull and interesting use of a common theme in this challenge. I love the way you use the grapes and plater to enhance the image. You have definately steped this them up a notch. I would liked to have seen a little more light on the grapes.  I also don''t particularly like the separation beteen table and wall. Overall this is a great shot keep up the nice work.', '2005-02-25 14:32:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1194422, 148189, 19010, '<td valign="top">very simple yet elegant It meets the challenge well. I do however see two thing I would like to change. First I thing a smoth backgroung would have worked better. And second the little bubbles in the glass detract from the overall beauty of the shot. I have heard (not tryed) that boiling the water first will help remove the bubbles. Still a great shot worthy of a 7. Keep up the nice work.</td>', 'very simple yet elegant It meets the challenge well. I do however see two thing I would like to change. First I thing a smoth backgroung would have worked better. And second the little bubbles in the glass detract from the overall beauty of the shot. I have heard (not tryed) that boiling the water first will help remove the bubbles. Still a great shot worthy of a 7. Keep up the nice work.', '2005-02-25 14:35:47.000000', NULL, 1),
